=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE package RakuAST::RatLiteral

=SUBTITLE Represent a literal rational number

    class RakuAST::RatLiteral { }

The C<RakuAST::RatLiteral> class represents a rational number (such as
`42.666`).

=head2 Object introspection

C<RakuAST::RatLiteral> objects are typically created when parsing Raku
Programming Language code.  So most developers will only need to know
how to introspect the objects created.

These introspection methods are available (in alphabetical order):

=head3 value

=begin code :preamble<my $literal>
say $literal.value;
=end code

The C<value> method returns the value it is representing.

=head2 Object creation

There is one way to create a C<RakuAST::RatLiteral> object directly
(rather than having C<RakuAST::Literal.from-value> figure it out):

=head3 new

=begin code
my $literal = RakuAST::RatLiteral.new(42.666);
say $literal.^name;  # RakuAST::RatLiteral
=end code

Creates a C<RakuAST::RatLiteral> object from the given value.
Assumes the value is really a C<Rat>, does B<not> do any sanity
checks.

=end pod
